# Claude Mistake Log
# Read at session start. Avoid every pattern below.
# On recurrence, increment "Repeat count" instead of adding a duplicate.
# At repeat count 2+, stop and change approach.
#
# Format:
# ## <short title>
# - Date:
# - What went wrong:
# - Root cause:
# - Fix:
# - How to avoid:
# - Repeat count: 1

(no entries yet)

## Fleet ship hull overlapped sand on sloped shore
- Date: 2026-11-03
- What went wrong: fleet ships clamped to water using shore() at the ship's centre x only; their ~40px half-length hull reached over the sand where the shore rises on the right.
- Root cause: copied the original cruise clamp (centre sample) for ships that get close to the shoreline.
- Fix: clamp y with the highest shore point sampled at x-40, x, x+40 (margin 21).
- How to avoid: when a wide sprite follows a sloped boundary, sample the boundary across the sprite's full extent, not just its anchor.
- Repeat count: 1

## Chose plain HTML/JS for a full app frontend without confirming the stack
- Date: 2026-11-03
- What went wrong: spec and first UI agent targeted plain HTML/vanilla JS; user wanted Next.js. Agent B work (tracker.html) was discarded.
- Root cause: copied the existing landing page stack (plain HTML) and assumed it for the dashboard.
- Fix: re-platformed to Next.js App Router + TypeScript; logic/store ported to src/lib.
- How to avoid: before specifying a multi-file app, state the proposed stack (framework, language, test runner) in the plan and use modern framework defaults for new frontends; do not inherit the stack of a one-off prototype page.
- Repeat count: 1

## Applied the landing-page pixel style to the whole dashboard; user wanted a professional colourful dashboard
- Date: 2026-11-03
- What went wrong: first tracker UI was muted pixel-art with a pixel font, hard shadows, dithering and static charts; user: "not professional, not colorful, no wow factor, no interactive charts, fonts look weird; prev dashboard pdf was better".
- Root cause: read "make it pixeled like the shore ship" as the style of every component, and never compared against the old dashboard the user already liked.
- Fix: SPEC_REDESIGN.md: Inter font, vibrant carrier palette, Recharts interactive charts, motion; pixel look kept only on the landing page.
- How to avoid: for a business dashboard keep brand art on hero/landing only, view the reference the user names (prev PDF/HTML render) BEFORE designing, and show a single-screen visual prototype before building all components.
- Repeat count: 1
